# K03 NS-ROLES-1 (Codex K03-S5-MIGRATION-20261007-06 (b), K03-S5-ALIAS-VISIBILITY-20261007-07; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# :666, :834, L2_spec_en.md:206): for absent b, `b: A` with A an existing Structure introduces b as a reference to A --
# no copy, no reparent: a write through b is a write of A.
# A named Structure is a callable, visible throughout the unit both ways (Codex -07 Q2): box above Later references
# Later, at the root and in a method above Later.  Exit 7; 81 / 82 if a write missed Later.
box: Later
box\v: 5
fn: m () int
    if: Later\v != 5
        return: 81
    inner: Later
    inner\v: 6
    if: Later\v != 6
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: m
Later:
    int: v 1
end: Later
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
